-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WWD 2020 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2020-11-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert Weber","x":"Segment earnings were negatively impacted by the lower sales volume, partially offset by cost reduction initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/19/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2020 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2020-11-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert Weber","x":"The decrease in R&D for both the quarter and the full year was primarily due to cost reduction initiatives and the divestiture of RPS.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/19/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2021-02-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert F. Weber","x":"The decline in segment earnings compared to the prior year was a result of lower volume, partially offset by cost reduction initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/01/woodward-inc-wwd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2021-02-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert F. Weber","x":"Industrial segment earnings increased primarily as a result of cost reduction initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/01/woodward-inc-wwd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q2","e":"wwd","d":"2021-05-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert F. Weber","x":"The decline in segment earnings compared to the prior year was the result of lower volume, partially offset by cost reduction initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/03/woodward-inc-wwd-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q2","e":"wwd","d":"2021-05-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert F. Weber","x":"The increase in Industrial segment earnings was primarily the result of cost reduction initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/03/woodward-inc-wwd-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2021-08-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Thomas A. Gendron","x":"So kind of related to the cost savings, we are beginning to get ramped back up from our shift standpoint, and that will cause us to bring back indirect labor into the form of supervisors, etc., etc. So we are seeing -- we have seen and are seeing increases there and anticipate we'll continue to…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/woodward-inc-wwd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2021-08-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Thomas A. Gendron","x":"So remain to be seen where we'll end up in terms of total systemic cost savings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/woodward-inc-wwd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2021-11-18","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Thomas A. Gendron","x":"Other parts of our business where we have shorter cycle, not LTAs or aftermarket, we do have the ability to have some price realization in those areas.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/18/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2021-11-18","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Thomas A. Gendron","x":"We're still able to get a reasonable price in the aftermarket, so we are seeing price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/18/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2021-11-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark D. Hartman","x":"Adjusted non-segment expenses for the fourth quarter of 2021 excludes the restructuring charges, adjusted non-segment expenses for the fourth quarter of 2020 primarily excludes the gain on sale of properties.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/18/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2021 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2021-11-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark D. Hartman","x":"It's mainly been on the direct labor side and some of that's been bringing back members that were laid off and then others are bringing in new members and getting them up and trained on the line overall.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/18/woodward-inc-wwd-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2025-07-28","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Dan Provaznik","x":"We remain vigilant and agile as we navigate tariffs, geopolitical matters, supply chain dynamics, and other expected and unexpected external factors.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/woodward-wwd-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2025-07-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bill Lacey","x":"The increase in segment earnings was primarily driven by price realization and higher volumes, supported by ongoing operational excellence and lean initiatives that enhance output and efficiency.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/woodward-wwd-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2025-07-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bill Lacey","x":"This expansion was driven by our progress in operational excellence, including price realization across the portfolio, and our ability to generate incremental margins from higher volumes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/woodward-wwd-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2025-11-24","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Charles P. Blankenship","x":"For example, this past quarter, we received more orders for spare end items than we anticipated, with trade and tariff uncertainty contributing to the order surge.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/24/woodward-wwd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2025-11-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"The improvement was driven by strong price realization and higher volume, partially offset by strategic investments in our aerospace manufacturing capabilities as well as inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/24/woodward-wwd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2025 Q4","e":"wwd","d":"2025-11-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"The 290 basis point improvement reflects solid price realization and higher sales volumes, partially offset by strategic investments in manufacturing capabilities, unfavorable mix, and inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/24/woodward-wwd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Kyle","x":"And I think it was Bill's commentary, you mentioned you guys have more confidence that this was prior under-provisioning rather than pull forward related to tariffs, say, in the prior year?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"So a 420 basis point improvement reflects solid price realization primarily driven by the new JDAM pricing, higher volumes, and favorable mix, primarily due to strong commercial services growth in the quarter, partially offset by strategic investments in manufacturing capabilities and inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"Within our core industrial business, margins expanded 200 basis points to 17.3% of core industrial sales driven by higher sales volume, strong price realization, and favorable mix, partially offset by inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Charles P. Blankenship","x":"And we've been working really hard to streamline the input process, the induction when a customer sends us a unit for repair or overhaul.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"So as it relates to the wind-down cost, we're expecting somewhere between $20 and $25 million of costs related to the restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q1","e":"wwd","d":"2026-02-02","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"Turning to our 2026 guidance, based on our strong start to the year, we are raising our 2026 guidance for sales and earnings and reaffirming the other elements of our full-year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/02/woodward-wwd-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q2","e":"wwd","d":"2026-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"While the strength in commercial services, higher commercial OEM volumes, and solid price realization drove meaningful margin expansion, this was largely offset by planned strategic investments to support future growth and inflationary pressures.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/woodward-wwd-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q2","e":"wwd","d":"2026-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William F. Lacey","x":"Within our core Industrial business, margins were approximately flat at 14.7% of core Industrial sales, as strong price realization and higher sales volume were partially offset by inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/woodward-wwd-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q2","e":"wwd","d":"2026-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Charles P. Blankenship","x":"All of these actions streamline and strengthen our portfolio and sharpen our focus on our most attractive near- and long-term growth opportunities.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/woodward-wwd-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2026-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Lacey","x":"The meaningful margin expansion was driven by strong price realization and increased leverage from higher sales volume, partially offset by inflation and unfavorable mix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/woodward-wwd-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WWD 2026 Q3","e":"wwd","d":"2026-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Lacey","x":"Price realization included a one-time retroactive pricing adjustment related to a contract that had been under negotiation for several quarters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/woodward-wwd-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1,7890,0,0,0,4944,2294],[36,1,9131,0,0,0,5470,2905],[37,1,6090,0,0,0,4109,1334],[38,1,7028,0,0,0,4792,1555],[39,1,7865,0,0,0,5716,1420],[40,1,6837,0,0,0,5154,1127],[41,1,7830,0,0,0,5677,1583],[42,1,7639,0,0,0,6087,1016],[43,1,8334,0,0,0,6203,1614],[44,1,7989,0,0,0,5362,1911],[45,1,8110,0,0,0,5401,2004],[46,1,9459,0,0,0,5258,3533],[47,1,7820,0,0,0,5732,1431],[62,1,8085,0,0,0,5432,2100],[63,1,7391,0,0,0,2354,3969],[64,1,7268,0,0,0,5058,1598],[65,1,4889,0,0,0,3969,605],[66,1,6772,0,0,0,4939,1445]],"cinema":[[35,1,7890,0,0,0,4944,2294],[36,1,9131,0,0,0,5470,2905]